Task 7 (the web API) is committed as `8ae1340`, and a reviewer is checking it now. All 83 tests pass in each of the three time zones.

The clock test does what it's meant to. The implementer swapped the real time into the booking, mentors and slots routes in turn, and the test failed each time.

One decision I'm waiting on the reviewer for: an oversized request body currently comes back as a server error. It's really bad input, so I've asked whether it should be a "validation failed" error instead. The implementer also made three small additions beyond the plan, which the reviewer is judging:
- a request with no body reports every missing field;
- short custom error messages on four checks;
- a guard against sending an error after the response has already gone out.

